      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we start by understanding her walking rate. Jana takes 24 minutes to walk one mile. We need to find out how many miles she can walk in 10 minutes.\n\nFirst, we calculate her walking rate in miles per minute:\n\\[\n\\text{Walking rate} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} = \\frac{1}{24} \\text{ miles per minute}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use her walking rate to find out how far she can walk in 10 minutes:\n\\[\n\\text{Distance in 10 minutes} = \\text{Walking rate} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{1}{24} \\times 10\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{24} \\times 10 = \\frac{10}{24}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify \\(\\frac{10}{24}\\), we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 10 and 24, which is 2:\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} = \\frac{10 \\div 2}{24 \\div 2} = \\frac{5}{12}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we convert \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) to a decimal. Performing the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{12} \\approx 0.416667\n\\]\n\nRounding 0.416667 to the nearest tenth, we get:\n\\[\n0.416667 \\approx 0.4\n\\]\n\nThus, Jana will walk \\(\\boxed{0.4}\\) miles in 10 minutes.",
